{"id":"kc.biology.molecular-basis-of-inheritance.fact-many-times-the-translation-can-50","v":2,"subject":"biology","chapterKey":"biology.molecular-basis-of-inheritance","chapter":"Molecular Basis of Inheritance","unit":"Genetics and Evolution","kind":"fact","front":"Why can transcription and translation be coupled in bacteria?","back":"In bacteria, since the mRNA does not require any processing to become active, and also since transcription and translation take place in the same compartment (there is no separation of cytosol and nucleus in bacteria), many times the translation can begin much before the mRNA is fully transcribed. Consequently, the transcription and translation can be coupled in bacteria.","quote":"In bacteria, since the mRNA does not require any processing to become active, and also since transcription and translation take place in the same compartment (there is no separation of cytosol and nucleus in bacteria), many times the translation can begin much before the mRNA is fully transcribed. Consequently, the transcription and translation can be coupled in bacteria.","blanks":[],"source":{"kind":"ncert","book":"Biology","code":"lebo105","chapterNo":5,"page":94,"section":"5.5.3 Types of RNA and the process of Transcription"},"importance":"good","asked":0,"tags":[],"order":960},
{"id":"kc.biology.molecular-basis-of-inheritance.fact-there-are-at-least-three-51","v":1,"subject":"biology","chapterKey":"biology.molecular-basis-of-inheritance","chapter":"Molecular Basis of Inheritance","unit":"Genetics and Evolution","kind":"fact","front":"How many RNA polymerases are there in the eukaryotic nucleus?","back":"There are at least three RNA polymerases in the nucleus (in addition to the RNA polymerase found in the organelles). There is a clear cut division of labour.","quote":"There are at least three RNA polymerases in the nucleus (in addition to the RNA polymerase found in the organelles). There is a clear cut division of labour.","blanks":[],"source":{"kind":"ncert","book":"Biology","code":"lebo105","chapterNo":5,"page":94,"section":"5.5.3 Types of RNA and the process of Transcription"},"importance":"must","asked":0,"tags":[],"order":970},
