{"id":"kc.biology.molecular-basis-of-inheritance.fact-which-is-primarily-responsible-for-78","v":2,"subject":"biology","chapterKey":"biology.molecular-basis-of-inheritance","chapter":"Molecular Basis of Inheritance","unit":"Genetics and Evolution","kind":"fact","front":"What is beta-galactosidase primarily responsible for?","back":"The z gene codes for beta-galactosidase (β-gal), which is primarily responsible for the hydrolysis of the disaccharide, lactose into its monomeric units, galactose and glucose.","quote":"The z gene codes for beta-galactosidase (β-gal), which is primarily responsible for the hydrolysis of the disaccharide, lactose into its monomeric units, galactose and glucose.","blanks":[],"source":{"kind":"ncert","book":"Biology","code":"lebo105","chapterNo":5,"page":100,"section":"5.8.1 The Lac operon"},"importance":"must","asked":0,"tags":[],"order":1460},
