{"id":"kc.biology.molecular-basis-of-inheritance.kl-the-a-gene-encodes-a-41","v":1,"subject":"biology","chapterKey":"biology.molecular-basis-of-inheritance","chapter":"Molecular Basis of Inheritance","unit":"Genetics and Evolution","kind":"key_line","front":"The a gene encodes a ____.","back":"The a gene encodes a transacetylase.","quote":"The a gene encodes a transacetylase.","blanks":["transacetylase"],"source":{"kind":"ncert","book":"Biology","code":"lebo105","chapterNo":5,"page":100,"section":"5.8.1 The Lac operon"},"importance":"must","asked":0,"tags":[],"order":1480},
{"id":"kc.biology.molecular-basis-of-inheritance.fact-hence-all-the-three-gene-79","v":1,"subject":"biology","chapterKey":"biology.molecular-basis-of-inheritance","chapter":"Molecular Basis of Inheritance","unit":"Genetics and Evolution","kind":"fact","front":"Why are all three gene products of the lac operon needed?","back":"Hence, all the three gene products in lac operon are required for metabolism of lactose.","quote":"Hence, all the three gene products in lac operon are required for metabolism of lactose.","blanks":[],"source":{"kind":"ncert","book":"Biology","code":"lebo105","chapterNo":5,"page":100,"section":"5.8.1 The Lac operon"},"importance":"good","asked":0,"tags":[],"order":1490},
{"id":"kc.biology.molecular-basis-of-inheritance.fact-lactose-is-the-substrate-for-80","v":1,"subject":"biology","chapterKey":"biology.molecular-basis-of-inheritance","chapter":"Molecular Basis of Inheritance","unit":"Genetics and Evolution","kind":"fact","front":"Which substance is the inducer of the lac operon, and why?","back":"Lactose is the substrate for the enzyme beta-galactosidase and it regulates switching on and off of the operon. Hence, it is termed as inducer.","quote":"Lactose is the substrate for the enzyme beta-galactosidase and it regulates switching on and off of the operon. Hence, it is termed as inducer.","blanks":[],"source":{"kind":"ncert","book":"Biology","code":"lebo105","chapterNo":5,"page":101,"section":"5.8.1 The Lac operon"},"importance":"must","asked":0,"tags":[],"order":1500},
{"id":"kc.biology.molecular-basis-of-inheritance.fact-the-repressor-of-the-operon-81","v":1,"subject":"biology","chapterKey":"biology.molecular-basis-of-inheritance","chapter":"Molecular Basis of Inheritance","unit":"Genetics and Evolution","kind":"fact","front":"Lac operon: what does the repressor do when no inducer is present?","back":"The repressor of the operon is synthesised (all-the-time – constitutively) from the i gene. The repressor protein binds to the operator region of the operon and prevents RNA polymerase from transcribing the operon.","quote":"The repressor of the operon is synthesised (all-the-time – constitutively) from the i gene. The repressor protein binds to the operator region of the operon and prevents RNA polymerase from transcribing the operon.","blanks":[],"source":{"kind":"ncert","book":"Biology","code":"lebo105","chapterNo":5,"page":101,"section":"5.8.1 The Lac operon"},"importance":"good","asked":0,"tags":[],"order":1510},
{"id":"kc.biology.molecular-basis-of-inheritance.fact-in-the-presence-of-an-82","v":1,"subject":"biology","chapterKey":"biology.molecular-basis-of-inheritance","chapter":"Molecular Basis of Inheritance","unit":"Genetics and Evolution","kind":"fact","front":"Lac operon: what happens to the repressor when an inducer is present?","back":"In the presence of an inducer, such as lactose or allolactose, the repressor is inactivated by interaction with the inducer. This allows RNA polymerase access to the promoter and transcription proceeds","quote":"In the presence of an inducer, such as lactose or allolactose, the repressor is inactivated by interaction with the inducer. This allows RNA polymerase access to the promoter and transcription proceeds","blanks":[],"source":{"kind":"ncert","book":"Biology","code":"lebo105","chapterNo":5,"page":101,"section":"5.8.1 The Lac operon"},"importance":"must","asked":0,"tags":[],"order":1520},
{"id":"kc.biology.molecular-basis-of-inheritance.fact-remember-glucose-or-galactose-cannot-83","v":1,"subject":"biology","chapterKey":"biology.molecular-basis-of-inheritance","chapter":"Molecular Basis of Inheritance","unit":"Genetics and Evolution","kind":"fact","front":"Can glucose or galactose act as inducers for the lac operon?","back":"Remember, glucose or galactose cannot act as inducers for lac operon.","quote":"Remember, glucose or galactose cannot act as inducers for lac operon.","blanks":[],"source":{"kind":"ncert","book":"Biology","code":"lebo105","chapterNo":5,"page":101,"section":"5.8.1 The Lac operon"},"importance":"good","asked":0,"tags":[],"order":1530},
{"id":"kc.biology.molecular-basis-of-inheritance.fact-a-very-low-level-of-84","v":2,"subject":"biology","chapterKey":"biology.molecular-basis-of-inheritance","chapter":"Molecular Basis of Inheritance","unit":"Genetics and Evolution","kind":"fact","front":"Why must a very low level of lac operon expression be present all the time?","back":"In the absence of a preferred carbon source such as glucose, if lactose is provided in the growth medium of the bacteria, the lactose is transported into the cells through the action of permease (Remember, a very low level of expression of lac operon has to be present in the cell all the time, otherwise lactose cannot enter the cells).","quote":"In the absence of a preferred carbon source such as glucose, if lactose is provided in the growth medium of the bacteria, the lactose is transported into the cells through the action of permease (Remember, a very low level of expression of lac operon has to be present in the cell all the time, otherwise lactose cannot enter the cells).","blanks":[],"source":{"kind":"ncert","book":"Biology","code":"lebo105","chapterNo":5,"page":101,"section":"5.8.1 The Lac operon"},"importance":"good","asked":0,"tags":[],"order":1540},
{"id":"kc.biology.molecular-basis-of-inheritance.kl-regulation-of-lac-operon-by-42","v":1,"subject":"biology","chapterKey":"biology.molecular-basis-of-inheritance","chapter":"Molecular Basis of Inheritance","unit":"Genetics and Evolution","kind":"key_line","front":"Regulation of lac operon by repressor is referred to as ____.","back":"Regulation of lac operon by repressor is referred to as negative regulation.","quote":"Regulation of lac operon by repressor is referred to as negative regulation.","blanks":["negative regulation"],"source":{"kind":"ncert","book":"Biology","code":"lebo105","chapterNo":5,"page":101,"section":"5.8.1 The Lac operon"},"importance":"must","asked":0,"tags":[],"order":1550},
{"id":"kc.biology.molecular-basis-of-inheritance.fact-essentially-regulation-of-lac-operon-85","v":1,"subject":"biology","chapterKey":"biology.molecular-basis-of-inheritance","chapter":"Molecular Basis of Inheritance","unit":"Genetics and Evolution","kind":"fact","front":"How can regulation of the lac operon also be visualised?","back":"Essentially, regulation of lac operon can also be visualised as regulation of enzyme synthesis by its substrate.","quote":"Essentially, regulation of lac operon can also be visualised as regulation of enzyme synthesis by its substrate.","blanks":[],"source":{"kind":"ncert","book":"Biology","code":"lebo105","chapterNo":5,"page":101,"section":"5.8.1 The Lac operon"},"importance":"must","asked":0,"tags":[],"order":1560},
{"id":"kc.biology.molecular-basis-of-inheritance.fact-a-very-ambitious-project-of-86","v":2,"subject":"biology","chapterKey":"biology.molecular-basis-of-inheritance","chapter":"Molecular Basis of Inheritance","unit":"Genetics and Evolution","kind":"fact","front":"In which year was the project of sequencing the human genome launched?","back":"With the establishment of genetic engineering techniques where it was possible to isolate and clone any piece of DNA and availability of simple and fast techniques for determining DNA sequences, a very ambitious project of sequencing human genome was launched in the year 1990.","quote":"With the establishment of genetic engineering techniques where it was possible to isolate and clone any piece of DNA and availability of simple and fast techniques for determining DNA sequences, a very ambitious project of sequencing human genome was launched in the year 1990.","blanks":[],"source":{"kind":"ncert","book":"Biology","code":"lebo105","chapterNo":5,"page":102,"section":"5.9 Human Genome Project"},"importance":"good","asked":0,"tags":[],"order":1570},
{"id":"kc.biology.molecular-basis-of-inheritance.kl-hgp-was-closely-associated-with-43","v":1,"subject":"biology","chapterKey":"biology.molecular-basis-of-inheritance","chapter":"Molecular Basis of Inheritance","unit":"Genetics and Evolution","kind":"key_line","front":"HGP was closely associated with the rapid development of a new area in biology called ____.","back":"HGP was closely associated with the rapid development of a new area in biology called Bioinformatics.","quote":"HGP was closely associated with the rapid development of a new area in biology called Bioinformatics.","blanks":["Bioinformatics"],"source":{"kind":"ncert","book":"Biology","code":"lebo105","chapterNo":5,"page":102,"section":"5.9 Human Genome Project"},"importance":"good","asked":0,"tags":[],"order":1580},
{"id":"kc.biology.molecular-basis-of-inheritance.list-identify-all-the-approximately-20-8","v":1,"subject":"biology","chapterKey":"biology.molecular-basis-of-inheritance","chapter":"Molecular Basis of Inheritance","unit":"Genetics and Evolution","kind":"list","front":"Name the goals of the Human Genome Project.","back":"Identify all the approximately 20,000-25,000 genes in human DNA\nDetermine the sequences of the 3 billion chemical base pairs that make up human DNA\nStore this information in databases\nImprove tools for data analysis\nTransfer related technologies to other sectors, such as industries\nAddress the ethical, legal, and social issues (ELSI) that may arise from the project","quote":"Identify all the approximately 20,000-25,000 genes in human DNA; (ii) Determine the sequences of the 3 billion chemical base pairs that make up human DNA; (iiii) Store this information in databases; (iv) Improve tools for data analysis; (v) Transfer related technologies to other sectors, such as industries; (vi) Address the ethical, legal, and social issues (ELSI) that may arise from the project.","blanks":[],"source":{"kind":"ncert","book":"Biology","code":"lebo105","chapterNo":5,"page":102,"section":"5.9 Human Genome Project"},"importance":"must","asked":0,"tags":[],"order":1590},
{"id":"kc.biology.molecular-basis-of-inheritance.fact-the-human-genome-project-was-87","v":1,"subject":"biology","chapterKey":"biology.molecular-basis-of-inheritance","chapter":"Molecular Basis of Inheritance","unit":"Genetics and Evolution","kind":"fact","front":"Which bodies coordinated the Human Genome Project, and for how long?","back":"The Human Genome Project was a 13-year project coordinated by the U.S. Department of Energy and the National Institute of Health.","quote":"The Human Genome Project was a 13-year project coordinated by the U.S. Department of Energy and the National Institute of Health.","blanks":[],"source":{"kind":"ncert","book":"Biology","code":"lebo105","chapterNo":5,"page":102,"section":"5.9 Human Genome Project"},"importance":"must","asked":0,"tags":[],"order":1600},
